/P 55 0 R
/T (Given p > q, the probability drops exponentially as z increases. In this system, with NFTcapped hash power, q is limited by the fraction of dishonest NFTs, enhancing resistance to 51% attacks. For example, if dishonest nodes control 30% of NFTs, q = 0.3, p = 0.7, and for z = 6 \(30 minutes confirmation\), the attack probability is approximately 0.00024. )
/E (Given p > q, the probability drops exponentially as z increases. In this system, with NFTcapped hash power, q is limited by the fraction of dishonest NFTs, enhancing resistance to 51% attacks. For example, if dishonest nodes control 30% of NFTs, q = 0.3, p = 0.7, and for z = 6 \(30 minutes confirmation\), the attack probability is approximately 0.00024. )
